[{:db/id "f96d8b6a-e305-583b-9f12-0bde0306eb41" :answer/id #uuid "f96d8b6a-e305-583b-9f12-0bde0306eb41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4abb445a-53b1-5dac-8db1-19d2b720a47b" :answer-field/id #uuid "4abb445a-53b1-5dac-8db1-19d2b720a47b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["f96d8b6a-e305-583b-9f12-0bde0306eb41"] :answer-field/correct "f96d8b6a-e305-583b-9f12-0bde0306eb41" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "6af2d8cd-fb27-51d6-805e-b4b55efe8db1" :answer/id #uuid "6af2d8cd-fb27-51d6-805e-b4b55efe8db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d13464d6-06b5-572e-a588-9d420ee2218d" :answer-field/id #uuid "d13464d6-06b5-572e-a588-9d420ee2218d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["6af2d8cd-fb27-51d6-805e-b4b55efe8db1"] :answer-field/correct "6af2d8cd-fb27-51d6-805e-b4b55efe8db1" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7b0730ae-94df-51c2-9122-80a657d5c130" :question/id #uuid "7b0730ae-94df-51c2-9122-80a657d5c130" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{6s + 7t = -17; -s + 5t = 9$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $6$, while in the second equation it is $-1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $6$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{6s + 7t = -17; (-s + 5t = 9) \\cdot (6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6s + 7t &= -17 \\\\\n-6s + 30t &= 54 \\\\\n(7t + 30t) &= (-17 + 54) \\\\\n37t &= 37 \\\\\nt &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = 1$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-s + 5t &= 9 \\\\\n-s + 5(1) &= 9 \\\\\n-s + 5 &= 9 \\\\\ns &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-4, \\,t=1$, which can be expressed as $(-4,1)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["4abb445a-53b1-5dac-8db1-19d2b720a47b" "d13464d6-06b5-572e-a588-9d420ee2218d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb" :answer/id #uuid "0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f538230e-e945-5377-a73a-dcace5a3652d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f538230e-e945-5377-a73a-dcace5a3652d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb"] :answer-field/correct "0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "12813af6-c484-54ac-9bee-0b9a07a1472c" :answer/id #uuid "12813af6-c484-54ac-9bee-0b9a07a1472c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "23b567cb-7d1b-5181-9ccc-bcb98c7d98fc" :answer-field/id #uuid "23b567cb-7d1b-5181-9ccc-bcb98c7d98fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["12813af6-c484-54ac-9bee-0b9a07a1472c"] :answer-field/correct "12813af6-c484-54ac-9bee-0b9a07a1472c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d400f619-bf7d-5b12-8de8-ccc69c639d78" :question/id #uuid "d400f619-bf7d-5b12-8de8-ccc69c639d78" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{s + 3t = -14; 3s - t = -2$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(s + 3t = -14) \\cdot (-3); 3s - t = -2\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3s - 9t &= 42 \\\\\n3s - t &= -2 \\\\\n(-9t - t) &= (42 - 2) \\\\\n-10t &= 40 \\\\\nt &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = -4$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = -4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns + 3t &= -14 \\\\\ns + 3(-4) &= -14 \\\\\ns - 12 &= -14 \\\\\ns &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-2, \\,t=-4$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-4)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["f538230e-e945-5377-a73a-dcace5a3652d" "23b567cb-7d1b-5181-9ccc-bcb98c7d98fc"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "3d9aae26-9eaa-543f-ad73-d4b0cc4ce5d3" :answer/id #uuid "3d9aae26-9eaa-543f-ad73-d4b0cc4ce5d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(- \\frac{29}{5}, \\frac{8}{5})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "52ca360c-fb47-5f69-899f-de261ec2a7c5" :answer/id #uuid "52ca360c-fb47-5f69-899f-de261ec2a7c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{4}, - \\frac{5}{4})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f52d4e69-0b6e-526b-ab03-608e96f2bffd" :answer/id #uuid "f52d4e69-0b6e-526b-ab03-608e96f2bffd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5, -2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "22b8f003-4864-5c70-95fe-d2b3563f85ca" :answer/id #uuid "22b8f003-4864-5c70-95fe-d2b3563f85ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7, -2)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "329f0e6d-30d3-5076-b0f7-a3bfcc97b663" :answer/id #uuid "329f0e6d-30d3-5076-b0f7-a3bfcc97b663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{4}, - \\frac{3}{4})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4740f935-4cde-5928-81e3-2873eb56ade9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4740f935-4cde-5928-81e3-2873eb56ade9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["3d9aae26-9eaa-543f-ad73-d4b0cc4ce5d3" "52ca360c-fb47-5f69-899f-de261ec2a7c5" "f52d4e69-0b6e-526b-ab03-608e96f2bffd" "22b8f003-4864-5c70-95fe-d2b3563f85ca" "329f0e6d-30d3-5076-b0f7-a3bfcc97b663"] :answer-field/correct "f52d4e69-0b6e-526b-ab03-608e96f2bffd" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a75817b8-4e26-5edd-a706-c4d036e41293" :question/id #uuid "a75817b8-4e26-5edd-a706-c4d036e41293" :question/problem "Find the solution $(a, b)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{-5a - 7b = -11; -a - 3b = 1$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $a$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $-5$, while in the second equation it is $-1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-5$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-5$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-5a - 7b = -11; (-a - 3b = 1) \\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a - 7b &= -11 \\\\\n5a + 15b &= -5 \\\\\n(-7b + 15b) &= (-11 - 5) \\\\\n8b &= -16 \\\\\nb &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = -2$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-a - 3b &= 1 \\\\\n-a - 3(-2) &= 1 \\\\\n-a + 6 &= 1 \\\\\na &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=5, \\,b=-2$, which can be expressed as $(5,-2)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["4740f935-4cde-5928-81e3-2873eb56ade9"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "7242848c-3d45-59cd-b531-0ff9de9e07b8" :answer/id #uuid "7242848c-3d45-59cd-b531-0ff9de9e07b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "580f77f4-bb2d-5fe9-8c7a-de148eb78cf9" :answer-field/id #uuid "580f77f4-bb2d-5fe9-8c7a-de148eb78cf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["7242848c-3d45-59cd-b531-0ff9de9e07b8"] :answer-field/correct "7242848c-3d45-59cd-b531-0ff9de9e07b8" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3e215f69-7281-5f0a-b1ad-ca14eb46e414" :answer/id #uuid "3e215f69-7281-5f0a-b1ad-ca14eb46e414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9f423d74-9353-5d5c-8788-04c8f0bcc44d" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f423d74-9353-5d5c-8788-04c8f0bcc44d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["3e215f69-7281-5f0a-b1ad-ca14eb46e414"] :answer-field/correct "3e215f69-7281-5f0a-b1ad-ca14eb46e414" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "cd3b4b3f-b020-5169-9586-17768134232d" :question/id #uuid "cd3b4b3f-b020-5169-9586-17768134232d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{-4x + 5y = 10; x + 6y = -17$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-4x + 5y = 10; (x + 6y = -17) \\cdot (4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + 5y &= 10 \\\\\n4x + 24y &= -68 \\\\\n(5y + 24y) &= (10 - 68) \\\\\n29y &= -58 \\\\\ny &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -2$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + 6y &= -17 \\\\\nx + 6(-2) &= -17 \\\\\nx - 12 &= -17 \\\\\nx &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-5, \\,y=-2$, which can be expressed as $(-5,-2)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["580f77f4-bb2d-5fe9-8c7a-de148eb78cf9" "9f423d74-9353-5d5c-8788-04c8f0bcc44d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "64612dae-60be-5da8-a58f-b92a90c02672" :answer/id #uuid "64612dae-60be-5da8-a58f-b92a90c02672" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "25eacce8-21cd-5065-b87b-8364d07c64a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "25eacce8-21cd-5065-b87b-8364d07c64a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["64612dae-60be-5da8-a58f-b92a90c02672"] :answer-field/correct "64612dae-60be-5da8-a58f-b92a90c02672" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40" :answer/id #uuid "0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "82814543-c725-5b0a-b1ee-c015e7918acc" :answer-field/id #uuid "82814543-c725-5b0a-b1ee-c015e7918acc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40"] :answer-field/correct "0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "9719f6ce-a725-5fda-8dba-4e72f19011f6" :question/id #uuid "9719f6ce-a725-5fda-8dba-4e72f19011f6" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{8x + y = -12; 2x - 7y = -32$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $8$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{8x + y = -12; (2x - 7y = -32) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8x + y &= -12 \\\\\n-8x + 28y &= 128 \\\\\n(y + 28y) &= (-12 + 128) \\\\\n29y &= 116 \\\\\ny &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 4$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - 7y &= -32 \\\\\n2x - 7(4) &= -32 \\\\\n2x - 28 &= -32 \\\\\n2x &= -4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=4$, which can be expressed as $(-2,4)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["25eacce8-21cd-5065-b87b-8364d07c64a2" "82814543-c725-5b0a-b1ee-c015e7918acc"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :answer/id #uuid "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "491f86ca-62f3-5ea9-8428-178689de26c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "491f86ca-62f3-5ea9-8428-178689de26c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e"] :answer-field/correct "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :answer/id #uuid "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a0ddcf7e-8326-53ea-93be-7d843009b320" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ddcf7e-8326-53ea-93be-7d843009b320" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d"] :answer-field/correct "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "02c41293-f116-502f-be60-22954dd650e1" :question/id #uuid "02c41293-f116-502f-be60-22954dd650e1" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{-8x + 5y = 1; -2x - 7y = 25$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-8$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-8x + 5y = 1; (-2x - 7y = 25) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= 1 \\\\\n8x + 28y &= -100 \\\\\n(5y + 28y) &= (1 - 100) \\\\\n33y &= -99 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 25 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 25 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 25 \\\\\n-2x &= 4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-3)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["491f86ca-62f3-5ea9-8428-178689de26c2" "a0ddcf7e-8326-53ea-93be-7d843009b320"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d97fab02-f410-5d26-9830-684eabd5761d" :answer/id #uuid "d97fab02-f410-5d26-9830-684eabd5761d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4, 5)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2faf14ba-bba7-51c7-9edf-cecfc41c14b5" :answer/id #uuid "2faf14ba-bba7-51c7-9edf-cecfc41c14b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7, 17)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "341043a8-156f-5366-9a35-b7d38e44dfa3" :answer/id #uuid "341043a8-156f-5366-9a35-b7d38e44dfa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{14}, \\frac{10}{7})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9632d4fa-7a1a-5278-a13a-d1e219be729e" :answer/id #uuid "9632d4fa-7a1a-5278-a13a-d1e219be729e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(- \\frac{19}{4}, \\frac{25}{2})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4aedf174-56a2-5192-a1db-d3ba0e5fc303" :answer/id #uuid "4aedf174-56a2-5192-a1db-d3ba0e5fc303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1, 5)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c554ee94-9b1e-56b7-bcce-cdb86ae35436" :answer-field/id #uuid "c554ee94-9b1e-56b7-bcce-cdb86ae35436" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d97fab02-f410-5d26-9830-684eabd5761d" "2faf14ba-bba7-51c7-9edf-cecfc41c14b5" "341043a8-156f-5366-9a35-b7d38e44dfa3" "9632d4fa-7a1a-5278-a13a-d1e219be729e" "4aedf174-56a2-5192-a1db-d3ba0e5fc303"] :answer-field/correct "4aedf174-56a2-5192-a1db-d3ba0e5fc303" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d579d3ab-2a4e-5b62-a685-7b2b44091ebf" :question/id #uuid "d579d3ab-2a4e-5b62-a685-7b2b44091ebf" :question/problem "Find the solution $(s, t)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{8s + 6t = 22; 2s + t = 3$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $s$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $8$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{8s + 6t = 22; (2s + t = 3) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8s + 6t &= 22 \\\\\n-8s - 4t &= -12 \\\\\n(6t - 4t) &= (22 - 12) \\\\\n2t &= 10 \\\\\nt &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = 5$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = 5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2s + t &= 3 \\\\\n2s + (5) &= 3 \\\\\n2s + 5 &= 3 \\\\\n2s &= -2 \\\\\ns &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-1, \\,t=5$, which can be expressed as $(-1,5)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["c554ee94-9b1e-56b7-bcce-cdb86ae35436"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "364f9c8a-cb70-5cde-84ad-03c48868d69b" :answer/id #uuid "364f9c8a-cb70-5cde-84ad-03c48868d69b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9ae32b84-e095-5a2f-9172-81edb43c515f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae32b84-e095-5a2f-9172-81edb43c515f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["364f9c8a-cb70-5cde-84ad-03c48868d69b"] :answer-field/correct "364f9c8a-cb70-5cde-84ad-03c48868d69b" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "30017ff9-b626-5f0f-96bf-3f60d887385e" :answer/id #uuid "30017ff9-b626-5f0f-96bf-3f60d887385e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c437e509-1b3a-5a4b-872f-05ce93198e77" :answer-field/id #uuid "c437e509-1b3a-5a4b-872f-05ce93198e77" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["30017ff9-b626-5f0f-96bf-3f60d887385e"] :answer-field/correct "30017ff9-b626-5f0f-96bf-3f60d887385e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "66c662cf-af7a-5ce7-907d-2fc15145c8ec" :question/id #uuid "66c662cf-af7a-5ce7-907d-2fc15145c8ec" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{9a + 4b = 16; -3a - 4b = 8$\n\nFind the solution $(a, b)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $a$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $9$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $3$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $-9$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $9$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{9a + 4b = 16; (-3a - 4b = 8) \\cdot (3)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9a + 4b &= 16 \\\\\n-9a - 12b &= 24 \\\\\n(4b - 12b) &= (16 + 24) \\\\\n-8b &= 40 \\\\\nb &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = -5$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = -5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a - 4b &= 8 \\\\\n-3a - 4(-5) &= 8 \\\\\n-3a + 20 &= 8 \\\\\n-3a &= -12 \\\\\na &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=4, \\,b=-5$, which can be expressed as $(4,-5)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["9ae32b84-e095-5a2f-9172-81edb43c515f" "c437e509-1b3a-5a4b-872f-05ce93198e77"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a1f2ef5d-7d4c-5874-a963-39537f63090c" :answer/id #uuid "a1f2ef5d-7d4c-5874-a963-39537f63090c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4ad33376-4060-5d96-9e58-c7394afcbf4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad33376-4060-5d96-9e58-c7394afcbf4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["a1f2ef5d-7d4c-5874-a963-39537f63090c"] :answer-field/correct "a1f2ef5d-7d4c-5874-a963-39537f63090c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "f7d55bbb-17db-553d-bf14-bb89392e7ac8" :answer/id #uuid "f7d55bbb-17db-553d-bf14-bb89392e7ac8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a4fe934f-8389-5fa9-ac8c-55f6141852fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4fe934f-8389-5fa9-ac8c-55f6141852fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["f7d55bbb-17db-553d-bf14-bb89392e7ac8"] :answer-field/correct "f7d55bbb-17db-553d-bf14-bb89392e7ac8" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3848697a-49af-57cf-80a1-3aeaa90cbfd0" :question/id #uuid "3848697a-49af-57cf-80a1-3aeaa90cbfd0" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{2x + 3y = 1; 14x - 3y = -17$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $2$, while in the second equation it is $14$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-7$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $-14$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $14$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(2x + 3y = 1) \\cdot (-7); 14x - 3y = -17\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-14x - 21y &= -7 \\\\\n14x - 3y &= -17 \\\\\n(-21y - 3y) &= (-7 - 17) \\\\\n-24y &= -24 \\\\\ny &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 1$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3y &= 1 \\\\\n2x + 3(1) &= 1 \\\\\n2x + 3 &= 1 \\\\\n2x &= -2 \\\\\nx &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1, \\,y=1$, which can be expressed as $(-1,1)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["4ad33376-4060-5d96-9e58-c7394afcbf4f" "a4fe934f-8389-5fa9-ac8c-55f6141852fe"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "079d8e57-e723-5341-8dde-001d8b14de99" :answer/id #uuid "079d8e57-e723-5341-8dde-001d8b14de99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "aa48b9e4-f99c-585d-9f9c-fcfbc501054e" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa48b9e4-f99c-585d-9f9c-fcfbc501054e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["079d8e57-e723-