n.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["aa48b9e4-f99c-585d-9f9c-fcfbc501054e" "dc5d5aa6-a936-5fba-8da0-69bd505be987"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "fc181fc8-9703-58c0-a004-a3247d964adb" :answer/id #uuid "fc181fc8-9703-58c0-a004-a3247d964adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(- \\frac{1569}{82}, \\frac{66}{41})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4372d300-0380-515a-a5b7-c7ff3a05051f" :answer/id #uuid "4372d300-0380-515a-a5b7-c7ff3a05051f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-24, -3)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "86db7400-28e3-565a-b953-d96d40f7af0c" :answer/id #uuid "86db7400-28e3-565a-b953-d96d40f7af0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3, -3)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "04912936-0284-538a-a031-970ac8ce1261" :answer/id #uuid "04912936-0284-538a-a031-970ac8ce1261" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(- \\frac{1077}{16}, \\frac{123}{8})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "305a3950-6485-5d6d-9a0b-5b40b1148ce8" :answer/id #uuid "305a3950-6485-5d6d-9a0b-5b40b1148ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(- \\frac{1257}{41}, \\frac{201}{41})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "891fd9c0-9987-5b47-b883-682276b9d5c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "891fd9c0-9987-5b47-b883-682276b9d5c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["fc181fc8-9703-58c0-a004-a3247d964adb" "4372d300-0380-515a-a5b7-c7ff3a05051f" "86db7400-28e3-565a-b953-d96d40f7af0c" "04912936-0284-538a-a031-970ac8ce1261" "305a3950-6485-5d6d-9a0b-5b40b1148ce8"] :answer-field/correct "86db7400-28e3-565a-b953-d96d40f7af0c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "b3065a5a-e33d-5a8d-955c-b55d1f00fd62" :question/id #uuid "b3065a5a-e33d-5a8d-955c-b55d1f00fd62" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{-12x - y = 39; -2x - 7y = 27$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-12$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-6$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-12x - y = 39; (-2x - 7y = 27) \\cdot (-6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - y &= 39 \\\\\n12x + 42y &= -162 \\\\\n(-y + 42y) &= (39 - 162) \\\\\n41y &= -123 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 27 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 27 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 27 \\\\\n-2x &= 6 \\\\\nx &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-3,-3)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["891fd9c0-9987-5b47-b883-682276b9d5c4"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a45d5d1a-0ddd-57b6-94a4-fadb72cadada" :answer/id #uuid "a45d5d1a-0ddd-57b6-94a4-fadb72cadada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c9a7d8bf-c851-5b7c-950c-16ced188e9d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a7d8bf-c851-5b7c-950c-16ced188e9d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["a45d5d1a-0ddd-57b6-94a4-fadb72cadada"] :answer-field/correct "a45d5d1a-0ddd-57b6-94a4-fadb72cadada" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "5c67e1be-bd46-5ffa-8808-2973f101d188" :answer/id #uuid "5c67e1be-bd46-5ffa-8808-2973f101d188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "83a992ad-facb-5e3e-9fe4-d815a0ee6bea" :answer-field/id #uuid "83a992ad-facb-5e3e-9fe4-d815a0ee6bea" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["5c67e1be-bd46-5ffa-8808-2973f101d188"] :answer-field/correct "5c67e1be-bd46-5ffa-8808-2973f101d188" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "c26af310-f3be-5785-a8b6-74feb81edc70" :question/id #uuid "c26af310-f3be-5785-a8b6-74feb81edc70" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{21u - 4v = -25; 3u + v = -2$\n\nFind the solution $(u, v)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $u$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $21$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-7$, then the $u$-coefficient will become $-21$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $21$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{21u - 4v = -25; (3u + v = -2) \\cdot (-7)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n21u - 4v &= -25 \\\\\n-21u - 7v &= 14 \\\\\n(-4v - 7v) &= (-25 + 14) \\\\\n-11v &= -11 \\\\\nv &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $v = 1$. However, we still need to find $u$. To do this, we substitute $v = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3u + v &= -2 \\\\\n3u + (1) &= -2 \\\\\n3u + 1 &= -2 \\\\\n3u &= -3 \\\\\nu &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-1, \\,v=1$, which can be expressed as $(-1,1)$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["c9a7d8bf-c851-5b7c-950c-16ced188e9d5" "83a992ad-facb-5e3e-9fe4-d815a0ee6bea"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "bd5dcb71-ce6e-543f-8d84-cd26efc72f79" :answer/id #uuid "bd5dcb71-ce6e-543f-8d84-cd26efc72f79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{113}{9}, - \\frac{11}{9})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c9adc298-4dc0-5aaf-b90e-98f63bda9ce1" :answer/id #uuid "c9adc298-4dc0-5aaf-b90e-98f63bda9ce1" :answer/type :answer.